   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 548 of the laws of 2022 relating to authorizing the\ncity of New York to discontinue the use as parkland a portion of real property\nin the borough of Brooklyn and to transfer such lands to the metropolitan\ntransportation authority, to enable the New York city transit authority to\nconstruct in such areas new permanent at-grade station improvements and\npedestrian bridges, in relation to making technical amendments thereto",
    "basePrintNo": "S6726",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6726-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§3, 5 & 6, Chap 548 of 2022",
    "lawSection": "Parks",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6726\n\nSPONSOR: SALAZAR\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 548 of the laws of 2022 relating to authorizing\nthe city of New York to discontinue the use as parkland a portion of\nreal property in the borough of Brooklyn and to transfer such lands to\nthe metropolitan transportation authority, to enable the New York city\ntransit authority to construct in such areas new permanent at-grade\nstation improvements and pedestrian bridges, in relation to making tech-\nnical amendments thereto\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill will make technical corrections to Chapter 548 of the laws of\n2022 to correct typographical errors.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nMetes & bounds description of Permanent Easement described in Section\n3(Area B) to be transferred to the MTA:\n\n1. Page 3, Line 1: Add \"foot\" after \"one-hundred\" (missing word)\n\n2. Page 3, Line 10: Replace \"38.50' \" with \"35.80' \" (typo)\n\nMetes & bounds description of land to be dedicated as parklands\ndescribed in Section 5 (Area F)\n\n1. Page 6, Line 32: Change \"easterly\" to \"westerly\" (typo)\n\n2. Page 6, Line 52: Replace \"124.23' \" with \"146.23' \" (typo)\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill will make technical corrections to Chapter 548 of the laws of\n2022 to correct typographical error that are necessary so legislation\nmatches the actual and correct metes and bounds description of the park-\nland being alienated as set forth in the property survey and the final\neasements transferring the property rights;\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis bill is an amendment to Chapter 548 of the laws of 2022.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
